ons</p></li><li class="border-b border-line py-8 last:border-b-0 sm:px-6 sm:first:pl-0 lg:border-b-0 lg:border-l lg:first:border-l-0"><p class="text-[clamp(2.75rem,5.4vw,5rem)] font-medium leading-none">5 min</p><p class="mt-3 text-muted">Live data refresh</p></li></ul></div></section><section data-tone="paper" class="tone-paper py-[clamp(4rem,9vw,8rem)]"><div class="wrap"><div class="flex flex-col"><div class="grid-12 gap-y-6 border-t border-line py-[clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.5rem)] first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-4"><div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28"><span class="text-meta text-muted">(<!-- -->01<!-- -->)</span><h2 class="mt-2 text-[clamp(1.875rem,3.4vw,3rem)]">Overview</h2></div></div><div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-8"><div><p class="mb-5 max-w-[62ch] text-body last:mb-0">I built this because the official FIFA site makes it hard to answer two simple questions: what&#x27;s happening now, and what&#x27;s coming up. The information is spread over a dozen pages. This is the dashboard I wanted: one place for live and upcoming matches, team and player stats and group standings. Since I was already pulling the historical data, it also carries a model that predicts how the rest of the tournament plays out.</p></div></div></div><div class="grid-12 gap-y-6 border-t border-line py-[clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.5rem)] first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-4"><div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28"><span class="text-meta text-muted">(<!-- -->02<!-- -->)</span><h2 class="mt-2 text-[clamp(1.875rem,3.4vw,3rem)]">How the predictions work</h2></div></div><div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-8"><div><div role="img" aria-label="Architecture diagram" class="my-6 min-h-88 overflow-x-auto rounded-tile border border-line bg-white p-6 [&amp;_svg]:mx-auto [&amp;_svg]:h-auto [&amp;_svg]:max-w-full"></div>
<ol class="prose-list prose-ol mb-6 max-w-[62ch]">
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Team ratings.</strong> A Poisson attack and defence rating is fitted for every national team with scikit-learn, on 964 World Cup matches from 1930 to 2022. Teams with little or no history are calibrated against their FIFA ranking points, and a home-advantage term is learned from each match&#x27;s actual host nation.</li>
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Pre-tournament simulation.</strong> The ratings seed a Monte Carlo simulation of the whole bracket, run 50,000 times.</li>
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Live data.</strong> Once the tournament starts, the app pulls scores, penalty shootouts, the real knockout bracket, squads and player stats from FIFA&#x27;s public API, revalidated every five minutes.</li>
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Conditioning on reality.</strong> Everything already decided on the pitch is treated as fixed. Only the unplayed matches are re-simulated, so the odds reflect what has actually happened.</li>
</ol></div></div></div><div class="grid-12 gap-y-6 border-t border-line py-[clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.5rem)] first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-4"><div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28"><span class="text-meta text-muted">(<!-- -->03<!-- -->)</span><h2 class="mt-2 text-[clamp(1.875rem,3.4vw,3rem)]">What&#x27;s on screen</h2></div></div><div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-8"><div><ul class="prose-list mb-6 max-w-[62ch]">
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Matches in one place.</strong> Every fixture, live score and result.</li>
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Live analytics.</strong> Scoring intensity, goals, match status and a &quot;team of the day&quot; drawn from current form.</li>
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Team and player pages.</strong> Squads, live 2026 stats, historical form and FIFA rankings.</li>
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Qualification simulator.</strong> Win, draw and loss probabilities for every upcoming fixture.</li>
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Interactive bracket.</strong> Play out one ending of the tournament yourself, in the browser, on the same simulation engine the server uses.</li>
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Rankings and history.</strong> Power ratings, past tournaments and a full match archive.</li>
<li class="relative border-t border-line py-3.5 pl-7 first:border-t-0 first:pt-0 last:pb-0"><strong class="font-medium">Methodology page.</strong> The model explained in plain English, inside the app.</li>
</ul></div></div></div><div class="grid-12 gap-y-6 border-t border-line py-[clamp(2.5rem,5vw,4.5rem)] first:border-t-0 first:pt-0"><div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-4"><div class="lg:sticky lg:top-28"><span class="text-meta text-muted">(<!-- -->04<!-- -->)</span><h2 class="mt-2 text-[clamp(1.875rem,3.4vw,3rem)]">Built as an app</h2></div></div><div class="col-span-12 lg:col-span-8"><div><p class="mb-5 max-w-[62ch] text-body last:mb-0">The site ships a web manifest and icons, so it installs to a phone&#x27;s home screen and opens full-screen. Pages are statically fast and never more than a few minutes stale.</p></div></div></div></div></div></section><section data-tone="paper" class="tone-paper pb-[clamp(4rem,9vw,8rem)]"><div class="wrap grid gap-x-6 gap-y-10 md:grid-cols-2"><figure class="md:col-span-2"><div class="overflow-hidden rounded-card bg-ink/5"><img alt="The FIFA World Cup 2026 dashboard on a phone, showing scoring intensity, goals and matches" loading="lazy" width="1122" height="1402" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" class="h-auto w-full" style="color:transparent" sizes="(min-width: 1280px) 1200px, 92vw" srcSet="/_next/image?url=%2Fmockups-projects%2Fnew-fifaaa.jpeg&amp;w=640&amp;q=75 640w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmockups-projects%2Fnew-fifaaa.jpeg&amp;w=750&amp;q=75 750w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmockups-projects%2Fnew-fifaaa.jpeg&amp;w=828&amp;q=75 828w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmockups-projects%2Fnew-fifaaa.jpeg&amp;w=1080&amp;q=75 1080w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmockups-projects%2Fnew-fifaaa.jpeg&amp;w=1200&amp;q=75 1200w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmockups-projects%2Fnew-fifaaa.jpeg&amp;w=1920&amp;q=75 1920w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmockups-projects%2Fnew-fifaaa.jpeg&amp;w=2048&amp;q=75 2048w, /_next/image?url=%2Fmockups-projects%2Fnew-fifaaa.jpeg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75 3840w" src="/_next/image?url=%2Fmockups-projects%2Fnew-fifaaa.jpeg&amp;w=3840&amp;q=75"/></div></figure></div></section><section data-tone="ink" class="tone-ink grain relative py-[clamp(4rem,9vw,8rem)]"><div class="wr